Summary

Completed a SQLMap-focused lab involving SQL injection discovery, database enumeration, and credential extraction against a vulnerable web application.

The room focused on identifying injectable parameters, understanding how SQLMap automates exploitation, and using enumeration techniques to extract databases, tables, and user credentials from a MariaDB/MySQL backend.

What stood out most was seeing how quickly a single vulnerable parameter can escalate into full database visibility when proper input validation and security controls are missing.

